    "code_current_through_note": "eCode360 code date 2021-08-16. New Laws (19), none a Chapter 209 text amendment. Map amendments Ord. 2021-16 (2021-12-20) and 2026-3 (2026-10-26).",
    "checks": [
      "The zoning code has no accessory dwelling unit, accessory apartment or in-law provision",
      "A single-family detached dwelling has 'only one dwelling unit from ground to roof' (209-5). LR, LMR, MR, MHR and NCR list only the single-family detached dwelling as a housing type",
      "HR allows a two-family (twin or duplex) dwelling by right on an 8,000 sq ft lot, 80 ft wide, with a density cap of 10 units per gross acre (209-16B(11), 209-16E, Table 1A)",
      "Accessory buildings up to 500 sq ft and 16 ft high: 4 ft from side and rear lines and 10 ft from other buildings on the lot (Table 1). Larger ones 'shall meet the area and dimensional requirements for principal buildings' (209-12E(6))",
      "Accessory buildings stand in the side or rear yard only (209-34E). An accessory building attached to the house is part of the principal building and meets its yards (209-34A). No permit for an accessory building before the house (209-34B)",
      "HR accessory buildings: 5 ft from side and rear lines and 20 ft between buildings (Table 1A)",
      "OSP lists 'Other uses of the same general nature' (209-12.1B). No such clause in LR, LMR, MR, MHR or NCR",
      "500 sq ft and 16 ft are thresholds, not caps. A larger accessory building meets the principal building rules, up to 30 ft",
      "eCode360 text dates from 2021-08-16. Ask the township for any zoning text amendment adopted since then"
    ],
